==Indonesian==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|id|nl|Bijbel|t=Bible}}, from {{der|id|la|Biblia}}, from {{der|id|grc|βιβλία||books}}, plural of {{m|grc|βιβλίον||small book}}, originally a diminutive of {{m|grc|βίβλος||book}}, from {{m|grc|βύβλος||papyrus}} (from the ancient [[Phoenicia]]n city of ''[[Byblos]]'' which exported this writing material).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|id|/ˈbi.bəl/}}
* {{hyphenation|id|bi|bêl}}

===Noun===
{{id-noun|head=bibêl}}

# [[Bible]], [[bible]]
#: {{syn|id|Alkitab}}

====Usage notes====
Although {{m|id|Alkitab}} and {{m|id|Bibel}} are synonymous, the usages are different. Most Christian denominations prefer to refer to the Bible as {{m|id|Alkitab}}, while {{m|id|Bibel}} may have a negative interpretation as it is used to discredit it.

